# ---- learning-ai-service --------------------------------------------------------------
# The rules above are deliberately broad — `*.txt`, `*.md`, `tests/`, `docs/` — because the
# repository root is full of client documents and scratch files. Applied to a Python service
# they would silently drop its dependency manifests and its entire test suite, which is how a
# checkout ends up unbuildable for reasons nobody can see. Named back in, file by file.
!learning-ai-service/requirements.txt
!learning-ai-service/requirements-test.txt
!learning-ai-service/README.md
# The Arabic system prompt is the product's behaviour written down — source, not a document.
!learning-ai-service/app/prompts/*.md
!learning-ai-service/tests/
!learning-ai-service/tests/**
!learning-ai-service/knowledge-samples/
!learning-ai-service/knowledge-samples/**

# Never the local virtualenv, the caches, or a downloaded model.
learning-ai-service/.venv/
learning-ai-service/.scratch/
learning-ai-service/**/__pycache__/
learning-ai-service/.pytest_cache/
learning-ai-service/.ruff_cache/
learning-ai-service/models/
